        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Embroidered flat, wallet shaped purse of canvas, embroidered with laid silver and silver-gilt thread and with polychrome silks, in tent stitch. The metal thread is laid across the entire surface of the purse and the silks are worked over it to produce a tapestry-like effect. The purse is stiffened, and lined with blue silk taffeta. The flap originally fastened with a loop and button, but the latter is missing.\nOn the front of the purse is a pastoral scene of sheep beneath a tree with a house, birds and outsized insects. On the back is a large house with trees, stags and birds.\nThe edges are bound with silver-gilt braid."@en , "Embroidered purse, France, 1700s."@en ;
